# Line endings, pinned (SPEC 15 §12.12 — the build must behave the same on the
# Windows CI runner as on a developer's machine).
#
# This file exists because two checks failed on Windows for the same reason and
# neither failure said so. Git's `core.autocrlf` checks files out with CRLF on
# Windows, so:
#
#   - `make-notices --check` compared a CRLF checkout against an LF generation
#     and reported that *every* package line had changed;
#   - a test that parses the ```json examples out of docs/formats.md found none,
#     because it searched for a newline the checkout does not have.
#
# Both were fixed at the point of comparison, which is correct and local. This
# makes the situation explicit for anything added later.

# Source and text: normalise to LF in the repository, and check out as LF
# everywhere. Tools that generate files write LF, so a CRLF checkout means every
# generated-file check fails for a reason unrelated to the file's contents.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.node binary
*.woff2 binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db binary
